SYMATTR Value {Ta}
TEXT 24 360 Left 1 ;FET 1
TEXT 216 360 Left 1 ;FET 2
TEXT 408 360 Left 1 ;FET 3
TEXT 600 360 Left 1 ;FET 4
TEXT -120 -160 Left 3 ;THERMAL MODEL - 150 W into N MOSFETs on the scrap heatsink
TEXT -120 -120 Left 1 ;Electrical analogue: 1 V = 1 degC, 1 A = 1 W, 1 ohm = 1 K/W, 1 F = 1 J/K.  V(Jn) = junction temperature.\nPer-FET current loops force equal current, and all drains see the same Vds, so power splits equally.\nRjc = 0.70 K/W (IRFP250N max).  Rcs = 0.5 K/W (TO-247 on a silicone/Kapton insulator + paste; 0.24 bare + grease).\nRsa: heatsink ~ 17 x 9 x 7 cm extruded audio-amp sink: ~0.9 K/W natural convection, ~0.25-0.35 K/W with a\n80-92 mm fan.  ESTIMATE ONLY - measure it (README, "heatsink characterisation").  Csa = 500 J/K ~ 0.55 kg Al.
TEXT -120 480 Left 2 !.param Ptot=150 N=4 Ta=30 Rjc=0.7 Rcs=0.5 Rsa=0.35 Csa=500\n.step param N list 2 3 4\n.step param Rsa list 0.25 0.35 0.5 0.9\n.tran 0 3600 0 2 startup\n.ic V(SINK)={Ta}\n.meas TRAN Tj_1h FIND V(J1) AT 3600\n.meas TRAN Tsink_1h FIND V(SINK) AT 3600\n.meas TRAN Tcase_1h FIND V(CASE1) AT 3600\n.meas TRAN t_sink_90pct_s WHEN V(SINK)=Ta+0.9*Ptot*Rsa
TEXT -120 760 Left 2 ;PASS: Tj <= 125 degC (50 degC margin to the 175 degC rating, which also keeps the derated DC SOA healthy).
